{"packet_id":"D010-01","doc_id":"D010","jurisdiction":"Boston, MA","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Boston Fair Chance policy — no blanket criminal-record denial","requirement":"Housing providers covered by the policy may not impose a blanket policy denying housing to anyone with arrests or convictions; they must consider applicants with criminal records on a case-by-case basis.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Housing providers receiving DND funding and/or land, or with income-restricted units created under the BPDA Inclusionary Development Policy; also applied to the Office of Fair Housing and Equity Affirmative Marketing Program.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Housing providers receiving DND funding or land, providers with BPDA Inclusionary Development Policy income-restricted units, and the Office of Fair Housing and Equity Affirmative Marketing Program"},"exemptions":"Does not apply to current criminal behavior; federal or state law imposing a conflicting criminal history requirement preempts the policy.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2017-02","citation":"Boston Fair Chance Tenant Selection Policy (Feb. 2017)","quoted_span":"Housing providers receiving Department of Neighborhood Development (DND) funding and/or land, or that have income restricted units created under the Boston Planning and Development Agency (BPDA) Inclusionary Development Policy will not impose a blanket policy that denies housing to anyone with arrests and or convictions. Housing providers will consider applicants on a case-by-case basis.","interaction":"Federal or state law imposing a conflicting criminal history requirement preempts this policy.","confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D010-01","doc_id":"D010","jurisdiction":"Boston, MA","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Boston Fair Chance policy — excluded criminal-record categories","requirement":"When deciding housing eligibility or considering eviction, providers may not consider arrests not resulting in conviction, convictions with judicial relief such as sealing or expungement, juvenile records, or convictions more than 5 years old.","key_value":"5-year conviction lookback","coverage_conditions":"Housing providers receiving DND funding and/or land, or with income-restricted units created under the BPDA Inclusionary Development Policy; also applied to the Office of Fair Housing and Equity Affirmative Marketing Program.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Housing providers receiving DND funding or land, providers with BPDA Inclusionary Development Policy income-restricted units, and the Office of Fair Housing and Equity Affirmative Marketing Program"},"exemptions":"Policy does not apply where there is a direct relationship between the conviction and the housing sought or an unreasonable risk of substantial harm to others; not applied to current criminal behavior; conflicting federal or state criminal history requirements preempt.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2017-02","citation":"Boston Fair Chance Tenant Selection Policy (Feb. 2017)","quoted_span":"a) Arrests that did not result in conviction. This includes dismissed charges, diversion programs, and similar non-convictions. b) Convictions that are subject to a form of judicial relief, such as expungement, sealing, and certificates for relief from disabilities. c) Juvenile records d) A conviction more than 5 years old.","interaction":"Federal or state law imposing a conflicting criminal history requirement preempts this policy.","confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D010-01","doc_id":"D010","jurisdiction":"Boston, MA","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Boston Fair Chance policy — credit score screening ban","requirement":"Housing providers may not use an applicant's credit score to approve or deny a housing application; credit history may be used only in lieu of rental history to judge ability to pay.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Housing providers receiving DND funding and/or land, or with income-restricted units created under the BPDA Inclusionary Development Policy; also applied to the Office of Fair Housing and Equity Affirmative Marketing Program.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Housing providers receiving DND funding or land, providers with BPDA Inclusionary Development Policy income-restricted units, and the Office of Fair Housing and Equity Affirmative Marketing Program"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2017-02","citation":"Boston Fair Chance Tenant Selection Policy (Feb. 2017)","quoted_span":"The agent agrees not to use the applicant credit score to approve or deny housing applications. b) Property Managers may consider an applicant’s credit history, but such information may ONLY be used in lieu of rental history to determine an applicant’s ability to pay rent when rental history is not available.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D010-01","doc_id":"D010","jurisdiction":"Boston, MA","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Boston Fair Chance policy — income and rental history verification","requirement":"An applicant's ability and willingness to pay must be shown by an identifiable source of sufficient income and prior rental history; lack of credit history, as opposed to poor credit history, is not sufficient justification to reject.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Housing providers receiving DND funding and/or land, or with income-restricted units created under the BPDA Inclusionary Development Policy; also applied to the Office of Fair Housing and Equity Affirmative Marketing Program.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Housing providers receiving DND funding or land, providers with BPDA Inclusionary Development Policy income-restricted units, and the Office of Fair Housing and Equity Affirmative Marketing Program"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2017-02","citation":"Boston Fair Chance Tenant Selection Policy (Feb. 2017)","quoted_span":"An applicant’s ability and willingness to pay rent must be demonstrated through an identifiable source of sufficient income to pay rent and prior rental history. The lack of credit history, as opposed to poor credit history, is not sufficient justification to reject an applicant.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
